
class Solution {
  public:

    /*
    PROBLEM: MAXIMUM SUM SUBARRAY OF SIZE K
    =======================================

    PROBLEM UNDERSTANDING:

    We are given an array and an integer k.

    We need to find the maximum sum of any contiguous
    subarray having exactly k elements.

    Example:

    arr = {2, 1, 5, 1, 3, 2}
    k = 3

    Possible subarrays of size 3:

    {2, 1, 5}  -> Sum = 8
    {1, 5, 1}  -> Sum = 7
    {5, 1, 3}  -> Sum = 9
    {1, 3, 2}  -> Sum = 6

    Maximum sum = 9


    APPROACH: SLIDING WINDOW (FIXED SIZE)
    ======================================

    Since we need a subarray of exactly k elements,
    we use a fixed-size sliding window.

    We maintain two pointers:

    i = starting index of the current window.
    j = ending index of the current window.

    STEP 1:
    Add arr[j] to the current window sum.

    STEP 2:
    Check whether the current window size is k.

    Window size = j - i + 1

    STEP 3:
    If window size becomes k:

        - Update ans with the current sum.
        - Remove the leftmost element arr[i] from sum.
        - Move i forward to remove that element
          from the current window.

    STEP 4:
    Move j forward to include the next element.

    Continue until the entire array is traversed.


    IMPORTANT VARIABLES:
    ====================

    n:
        Size of the array.

    ans:
        Stores the maximum sum of a subarray
        having exactly k elements.

    sum:
        Stores the sum of the current window.

    i:
        Starting index of the current window.

    j:
        Ending index of the current window.


    TIME COMPLEXITY:
    ================

    We traverse the array only once.

    Each element is added to the window once
    and removed from the window at most once.

    Time Complexity = O(n)


    SPACE COMPLEXITY:
    =================

    We use only a few extra variables.

    Auxiliary Space Complexity = O(1)
    */


    int maxSubarraySum(vector<int>& arr, int k) {

        // Store the size of the array
        int n = arr.size();

        // Stores the maximum sum found so far
        // Initialize with a very small value
        int ans = -1e9;

        // Stores the sum of the current window
        int sum = 0;

        // i represents the starting index
        // of the current window
        int i = 0;

        // j represents the ending index
        // of the current window
        int j = 0;


        // Traverse the array using j
        while(j < n){

            // Store the current element
            int ele = arr[j];

            // Add the current element to the window sum
            sum = sum + ele;


            // Check whether the current window
            // contains exactly k elements
            if(j - i + 1 == k){

                // Update the maximum sum
                // using the current window sum
                ans = max(ans, sum);

                // Store the leftmost element
                // of the current window
                int left = arr[i];

                // Remove the leftmost element
                // because we need to slide the window
                sum = sum - left;

                // Move the starting pointer forward
                i++;
            }

            // Move the ending pointer forward
            // to include the next element
            j++;
        }

        // Return the maximum sum of a
        // contiguous subarray of size k
        return ans;
    }
};
